# Expo Router Screen Patterns

Screens are thin wrappers that delegate to feature components in `src/components/`.

## Structure

```tsx
import { useLocalSearchParams } from "expo-router";
import { FeatureComponent } from "@/components/feature-name";
import { KeyboardAvoidingView, NavigationBar, SafeAreaView } from "@/uikit/core";

export default function Page() {
  const { paramName } = useLocalSearchParams<{ paramName: string }>();

  return (
    <SafeAreaView className="page">
      <NavigationBar title="Screen Title" />
      <KeyboardAvoidingView>
        <FeatureComponent />
      </KeyboardAvoidingView>
    </SafeAreaView>
  );
}
```

## Rules

- Always use `export default function Page()`
- Parse route params with `useLocalSearchParams<{ ... }>()`
- Wrap content in `SafeAreaView className="page"` with a `NavigationBar`
- Add `KeyboardAvoidingView` if the screen has inputs
- Keep screens thin -- all business logic belongs in the feature component under `src/components/`
- Layout files (`_layout.tsx`) use `Stack`, `Tabs`, or `Slot` from expo-router
